title: '`pallet-accumulate-and-forward`: measure the transfer period from the last forward'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `on_idle` only forwarded when the block number of the configured `BlockNumberProvider` was an
    exact multiple of `TransferPeriod`. A chain does not observe every block of that provider: with
    `RelaychainDataProvider` a parachain sees the relay chain block number advance in steps of two
    or more, so the check can be missed indefinitely. On Coretime Polkadot and Kusama a relay
    period of 600 fires once an hour on one parity and never on the other.

    The pallet now records the block of the last forwarding attempt in the new `LastForwardBlock`
    storage item and forwards once `now - last >= TransferPeriod`, so the cadence holds on any
    block cadence and runtimes can keep `BlockNumberProvider = RelaychainDataProvider`. No
    migration is needed: an empty `LastForwardBlock` means "never forwarded".

crates:
- name: pallet-accumulate-and-forward
  bump: minor
